{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "008C", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "\\begin{eqnarray*}\n(f_p\\mathcal{G})_x\n& = &\n\\colim_{x \\in U} f_p\\mathcal{G}(U) \\\\\n& = &\n\\colim_{x \\in U} \\colim_{f(U) \\subset V} \\mathcal{G}(V) \\\\\n& = &\n\\colim_{f(x) \\in V} \\mathcal{G}(V) \\\\\n& = &\n\\mathcal{G}_{f(x)}\n\\end{eqnarray*}", "MATH_0002": "$V$", "MATH_0003": "$Y$", "MATH_0004": "$f(x)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-lemma-colimits-commute}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:51490f5b7b1ef8cbf1c86d446bcbed5e8e01cf14e816e55c4b9d45975fddcd89", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d5ae29d51f6e388a75f078006b926e685a15f72503e889485bb6482654e10130", "source_text": "This you can see as follows\n<MATH_0001>\nHere we have used\nCategories, Lemma <REF_0001>,\nand the fact that any <MATH_0002> open in <MATH_0003> containing <MATH_0004>\noccurs in the third description above. Details omitted.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a3a8eed04bb1b5746b7666944ef2b1f951026314f6a9a83cdceefbf5fcaa0e90", "unit_id": "tag:008G:proof"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "008C", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0002": "$Y$", "MATH_0003": "$f^{-1}\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0004": "$$\nf^{-1}\\mathcal{G} = (f_p\\mathcal{G})^\\# .\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$f^{-1}$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\Mor_{\\Sh(X)}(f^{-1}\\mathcal{G}, \\mathcal{F})\n=\n\\Mor_{\\Sh(Y)}(\\mathcal{G}, f_*\\mathcal{F}).\n$$", "MATH_0007": "\\begin{eqnarray*}\n\\Mor_{\\Sh(X)}(f^{-1}\\mathcal{G}, \\mathcal{F})\n& = &\n\\Mor_{\\textit{PSh}(X)}(f_p\\mathcal{G}, \\mathcal{F}) \\\\\n& = &\n\\Mor_{\\textit{PSh}(Y)}(\\mathcal{G}, f_*\\mathcal{F}) \\\\\n& = &\n\\Mor_{\\Sh(Y)}(\\mathcal{G}, f_*\\mathcal{F})\n\\end{eqnarray*}", "MATH_0008": "$f_p$", "MATH_0009": "$f_*$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-f-map}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:06a2df6d86c4570c31abb8be490546410b5e5814a1b7acd5ad723e92c85b5fa7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9d78a1012445d5acca3073e291f4d1358cf46e1034c8c3023053ae75058376c9", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a sheaf of sets on <MATH_0002>.\nThe <TEXTITOPEN_0001>pullback sheaf<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> <MATH_0003> is defined\nby the formula\n<MATH_0004>\nThe pullback <MATH_0005> is a left adjoint of\npushforward on sheaves. In other words,\n<MATH_0006>\nNamely, we have\n<MATH_0007>\nFor the first equality we use that sheafification is a left adjoint\nto the inclusion of sheaves in presheaves. For the second equality\nwe use that <MATH_0008> is a left adjoint to <MATH_0009> on presheaves. We will return\nto this statement in the proof of Lemma <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ba15fa2ec18bde95c01afda9cae3e67300ca43de9f7081e1b76c5a9c1d0ce818", "unit_id": "tag:008C:prose-0004"}
