{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "008C", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$g : Y \\to Z$", "MATH_0003": "$(g \\circ f)^{-1}$", "MATH_0004": "$f^{-1} \\circ g^{-1}$", "MATH_0005": "$(g \\circ f)_p \\cong f_p \\circ g_p$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-pullback-composition}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9ffeb9c076ebf7140c7eb957366047b0a8b2ac158f4a990e9686335dce6fa514", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1c7366bcfc6b812743b825ba215282d9b64581eb6b742d535dbbdb48980112e7", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> be continuous maps\nof topological spaces. The functors <MATH_0003>\nand <MATH_0004> are canonically isomorphic.\nSimilarly <MATH_0005> on\npresheaves.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:80274f6d9e8864904cdf2281cab44af1be0367698e14c4be72d45f8a8cc8d7e9", "unit_id": "tag:008I:statement"}
